PrePoMax-X B022: SPOOLES 2.2's multithreaded factorization and solve on weakly ordered CPUs (ARM64).

SPOOLES hands fronts and solution blocks between threads through ChvList/SubMtxList and char flags. Lists with
one producer thread skipped their lock, and the lists' state and the solve's frontIsDone/IsDone flags were read
with plain loads. That is correct only under x86's ordered stores: on Apple Silicon a reader could see a list's
count reach zero before the object added last, and lose that aggregate (wrong eigenvalues in 3 of 8 runs).
The lists now always use their lock when they have one; the flags are release stores and acquire loads (GCC builtins).
Applied by ThirdParty/Build/calculix-cpu.py with patch -p1 in the SPOOLES source folder.

